# E2E Verification

Use automated checks before reporting UI/canvas/online work as done.

**Run `npm run test:e2e`, `npm run verify`, and other npm scripts inside the Dev Container** (not on the Windows host with bind-mounted `node_modules`).

## Commands

| Command | When |
|---------|------|
| `npm run test:unit` | Logic/model changes only |
| `npm run test:e2e` | UI, canvas, routing, Firebase online flows |
| `npm run verify` | Full agent check: format + unit + e2e + build |

## Selectors

Prefer stable `data-testid` attributes:

- `enter-local`, `enter-online` — home mode cards
- `mode-move`, `mode-draw`, `mode-erase` — toolbar modes
- `clear-all`, `load-image` — toolbar actions
- `canvas-stage` — Konva canvas wrapper
- `view-single`, `view-leader`, `view-follwer` — view sharing modes (`follwer` typo intentional)
- `invalid-room-key` — invalid/missing room key error page

Reuse helpers in `e2e/helpers.ts` (`goToLocalMode`, `drawStrokeOnCanvas`, `roomUrl`, `createOnlineRoom`, etc.).

## Online tests

E2E starts Firebase Emulator automatically via `npm run e2e:server` (Playwright `webServer`), or reuses a healthy dev server on port 3000.

Online rooms are created through the Emulator REST API (`e2e/helpers.ts`): POST room, PATCH `e2ee.check`, register `#k=` in `roomKeyHashes`. Navigate with `roomUrl(roomId)` (`/online?roomId=…#k=…`). Helpers decrypt RTDB snapshots via `src/crypto/roomCrypto.ts`.

Home-card click flows for keyed rooms are covered in `e2e/room-key.spec.ts`; API room creation covers most online specs.

First-time setup in Dev Container:

```bash
npm run test:e2e:install
sudo env "PATH=$PATH" npx playwright install-deps chromium
```

If Playwright reports missing browsers after host-side npm, run `npx playwright install chromium` inside the container.

## Failure artifacts

On failure, inspect:

- `playwright-report/index.html` — HTML report
- `test-results/` — screenshots and traces

## Scope guidance

- Canvas drawing: verify mode switch + stroke via `canvasHasRedStroke`
- Online room: prefer `createOnlineRoom` + `roomUrl` (keyed E2EE room), not URL without `#k=`
- Room key errors: `/errors/invalid_room_key` (`invalid-room-key`)
- Do not rely on browser MCP alone when `npm run test:e2e` can cover the flow
